{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/31150-compact-the-order-of-st-anthony-the-gravediggers","id":31150,"title":"Compact: The Order of St Anthony, The Gravediggers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-16T13:05:51-08:00","id":31150,"title":"Compact: The Order of St Anthony, The Gravediggers","content":"<div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:24px\">The Order of St Anthony</span><br /> <b>The Gravediggers</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Order of St Anthony can trace it's origins to a nameless network that began with the Stalinist purge of religion. As the churches and monasteries fell one by one priests and monks were driven into hiding. Some fled to other parts of the world but many more hid themselves with believers and sympathisers creating an underground rail-road of safehouses and secret churches.<br /> <br /> In time, Stalin's policies changed, and the Church was permitted to rebuild. The clergy emerged from hiding to resume their duties but not all was well in their absence. In the corruption and chaos of communism monsters had taken root and began to prey upon the people, and they did not like opposition. Almost as soon as the safehouse doors were closed, they opened once again to shelter priests targeted for speaking out. But this time it was no human enemy, there were no armies to enforce unjust laws, it was nothing but monsters. This time the clergy resolved to strike back.<br /> <br /> This life of hiding necessarily created a tightly-knit network among the clergy. In contrast to many compacts, the Order of St Anthony have a tight organisation and relatively firm hierarchy \u2013 the former a memory of life under Communism, the latter a side effect of the Church's own hierachy. Members of the group are kept in routine contact through a network of secret messages, and rarely keep secrets from one another.<br /> <br /> The monks and priests of St. Anthony have survived the communists, they survived the Great Patriotic War, and god willing they will survive even the immortal undead.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:20px\">The Enemy</span><br /> <br /> The truth is spoken across the steppes and preserved in old wives tales. Dead left unburied shall rise again. It's a pity that such words of warning never reached the corridors of power. The Great Patriotic War and the communist purges has resulted in mountains of dead, and undead. The Order of St Anthony know more about fighting the walking dead than any other kind of monster simply because they encounter them far more than any other kind of monster.<br /> <br /> To an outsider it might appear that the Order of St Anthony is polarised between those who believe the restless dead are victims to be helped and those who believe they are monsters to be purged with fire. The truth is the exact opposite, the hierarchy has led to a strict orthodoxy. The division of opinion is in fact a division of labour. Some gravediggers specialise in ghosts and revenants. Trapped spirits who need help returning to the proper heavenward path. Others specialise in vampires and mindless zombies, monsters fit only to be purged with fire. Necromancers fall into a grey area, they are given a chance to repent but only one chance.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Picture: A monk with an awesome beard walks towards the viewer. His robes are shredded, leaving his impressively muscular chest bare, though with one hand he holds the remains of his robes against a large bleeding wound. Fearsome ghosts surround him but he pays them no head.<br /> <br /> I shall not allow myself to die.<br /> While my duties remain unfulfilled.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Monasteries</span><br /> The Gravediggers divide themselves into the monastery where they studied. These are not actual monasteries, but code names used to hide shelters from the eyes of the communists. While older members may well have actually took shelter in the monastery they claim membership younger members think of them as schools of thought first and safehouses second.<br /> <br /> <b>The Monastery of Blood</b> are the most resolute of the Order, their mission is to face evil without fear and send it back to whatever hell it came from. Vampires, unrepentent necromancers and other monsters that cannot or will not turn from the path of evil are their pray.<br /> Speciality: Crafts (Firestarting)<br /> <br /> <b>The Monastery of Sweat</b> serve as the leaders and organisers of a large but loose network of supporters and sympathisers who in turn run the network of safehouses, secure messages and equipment caches. Members are not expected to face monsters directly, but often go into dangerous and unknown territory to prepare the ground.<br /> Speciality: Survival (Safehouses) or Streetwise (Safehouses)<br /> <br /> <b>The Monastery of Tears</b> take those monsters that can be redeemed, and somewhat specialise in ghosts. They heal the monster's emotional scars, bring justice to past crimes, and return the monsters to the grace of god.<br /> Speciality: Investigation (Records)<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Status</span><br /> <br /> For clergy, status in the Gravedigger's tends to go in hand-in-hand with their status in the Church itself. Lay members' status is more informal, although it is less likely to reach the higher levels.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Wherever you go the Order's network of safehouses is ready to shelter you. You gain a dot in the Safehouse merit, what's more you can hold this dot in reserve to instantly gain access to a safehouse when you most need it \u2013 the Gravediggers have a lot of sympathisers who will hide a hunter in the attic, no questions asked. At the end of a session you may choose to relinquish your free dot and place it back in reserve.<br /> <br /> *** Your name has travelled far among the Order's network of sympathiesrs. You have 2 dot in Allies applied to Order Supporters. Your supporters are rarely combatants, but excel in providing resources, information and a metaphorical smokescreen.<br /> <br /> ***** You have stared death itself in the eye, and after that nothing scares you. You gain the Merit: Fearless.<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\">Endowment: Strength of Will (O - OOOOO)</span><br /> The Order of St Anthony are survivors above all. They oldest among them still remember life under communist rule, even younger members have survived daily life dealing with the incomprehensible undead legacy from two of humanities darkest crimes. After that, there is little that can sway a Gravedigger from his path.<br /> <br /> All powers granted by Strength of Will cost 1 Willpower, last for one scene and can be activated reflexively, if they modify a roll they may be activated before the roll takes place. Remember that only one point of Willpower can be spent per turn.<br /> <br /> O: The Gravedigger may add resolve to all rolls to resist fear or temptation, this may result in counting resolve twice.<br /> OO: The Gravedigger reduces penalties from Wounds, diseases, and other weaknesses of the body by Resolve.<br /> OOO: The Gravedigger may add resolve when rolling to resit a supernatural powers that control or influence the mind or emotions, this may result in counting resolve twice.<br /> OOOO: The Gravedigger will not pass out from wounds, any other method to force the Gravedigger into unconsciousness must score more successes than her resolve to be successful.<br /> OOOOO: The Gravedigger gains temporary health equal to resolve.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Commentary: The Order of St Anthony came from the short lived project Grave Robbers which meant to do for Geists, Sin-Eaters, Ghosts and all other undead beasties what Night Stalkers did for vampires. The original idea and thus credit belongs to Sunless Nick. This is my interpretation. </span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">I wrote this a long time ago and only now posted it. I still quite like the themes, the ideas, but I think if I did it again I would make it a Conspiracy. Firstly I think it fits the themes of the Gravediggers better; rather than being born from recent events it could be far older and survived two painful catastrophes. That fits the survivalist themes better than being born during the bad times. Secondly it seems a little... wrong for a hierarchical group tied to the ancient, influential and wealthy Eastern Orthodox Church to be a Compact. Finally, I don't know why but I think there has to be a scene where the MM and the Gravediggers are raiding the same vampire's house, they both burst in on each other, and both cells are dopplegangers, like that <a href=\"http://www.megidish.net/wp-content/uploads/2011/07/shaun_of_the_dead_numbered1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">scene in Shawn of the Dead</a></span>.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">So Endowments; I'm actually thinking the should have Benediction but with a focus on defensive powers to fit the theme of Endurance. </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-17-2013, 07:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T13:58:02-08:00","id":31195,"title":"","content":"I quite like them! Short and to the point while still being thematic and meaty. One thing of note that may interest you; the Church is known to take in <i>krokodil</i> addicts and 'reform' them, with some rather militant branches being especially fond of it. The end result is zealots who are quite literally rotting from the inside out, so you have what are essentially angry Christian zombies. Worth looking into.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 12-16-2013, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T14:01:01-08:00","id":31200,"title":"","content":"Now that sounds fitting. How would you represent the post-addiction effects of krokodil mechanically? I know nothing about this drug.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T14:08:28-08:00","id":31208,"title":"","content":"From what I know, it's like super-heroin, but made from wretched stuff, and it basically causes you to rot. So however you would reflect &quot;chunks of the limb you injected it into necrotizing and sloughing off,&quot; would be accurate. I'm not sure if those limbs are later amputated, but it would make sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T17:51:25-08:00","id":31356,"title":"","content":"I like them, but I would like more umpf in their history. Some sort of intriguing catalyst for their formation seems to be missing. But I do love the Idea of an Eastern Orthodox rival to the MM! I agree that Benediction seems just as appropriate. In fact in my gameworld Benediction is plainly a Catholic secret magic period, not just one used to hunt Vampires. So you may have members of say the Hospitaller Knights using it to heal in their Free Hospitals where they serve the poor and sick. The Ghoul master of the MM just made the point of weaponizing these holy miracles, where the rest of the church only uses it among their most sacred orders, including Monks/Knights/Exorcists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T02:03:11-08:00","id":31553,"title":"","content":"The basic concept is pretty good though I think the history is kinda off. The nations incorporated into the post-war Eastern Bloc were mostly none-Orthodox; the actual Orthodox countries were generally already republics of the USSR. Further, the Great Patriotic War was the point at which Stalin and the Communist state came to an arrangement with the Church allowing it to start rebuilding; the persecution of the church was generally in the twenties and thirties, and even then I don't think it was ever actually banned, there were always a couple of hundred churches still open.<br /> <br /> That said, I kinda like the idea of running a ghost-hunting game during the Stalinist purges (as horribly insensitive as that sounds). Putting the unjustly murdered to rest, while dodging the attention of the OGPU, or maybe coming to an arrangement with them, as morally compromising as that may be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-17T04:06:10-08:00","id":31576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/31150-compact-the-order-of-st-anthony-the-gravediggers?p=31553#post31553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The basic concept is pretty good though I think the history is kinda off. The nations incorporated into the post-war Eastern Bloc were mostly none-Orthodox; the actual Orthodox countries were generally already republics of the USSR. Further, the Great Patriotic War was the point at which Stalin and the Communist state came to an arrangement with the Church allowing it to start rebuilding; the persecution of the church was generally in the twenties and thirties, and even then I don't think it was ever actually banned, there were always a couple of hundred churches still open.</div> </div> </div> </div> Thank Micahel. You're completely right, the history needs fixing. Fortunately the Compact works just as well with the correct history so I can fix that easily.<br /> <br /> I made a quick edit to fix the history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/31150-compact-the-order-of-st-anthony-the-gravediggers?p=31553#post31553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I kinda like the idea of running a ghost-hunting game during the Stalinist purges (as horribly insensitive as that sounds). Putting the unjustly murdered to rest, while dodging the attention of the OGPU, or maybe coming to an arrangement with them, as morally compromising as that may be.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't sound that insensitive to me.<br /> <br /> Anyway this does give me at least one idea (for the Conspiracy version, not the Compact), that part of Stalin's arrangement with the Church included a complete ban on the church operating it's own militia. I think that adding a period of suppression would help the themes. Suppression fits with Endurance because, well it lasts longer, being shot just kills you.<br /> <br /> It also means that the EOC Hunters operating in defiance of the agreement wouldn't be able to do more than chip away at the growing number of undead leading to a nice enormous horde for PCs to worry about in modern games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/31150-compact-the-order-of-st-anthony-the-gravediggers?p=31356#post31356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like them, but I would like more umpf in their history. Some sort of intriguing catalyst for their formation seems to be missing.</div> </div> </div> </div> Got any ideas? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Hmmm, I wonder if anyone here actually is Eastern Orthodox?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/31150-compact-the-order-of-st-anthony-the-gravediggers?p=31356#post31356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact in my gameworld Benediction is plainly a Catholic secret magic period, not just one used to hunt Vampires. So you may have members of say the Hospitaller Knights using it to heal in their Free Hospitals where they serve the poor and sick. The Ghoul master of the MM just made the point of weaponizing these holy miracles, where the rest of the church only uses it among their most sacred orders, including Monks/Knights/Exorcists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do something similar. To me Longius and Athanasius are the same order, by far the largest, and have the looming Longius vs Athanasius war as an internal matter. This leaves room for the Sisterhood of St Wisdom to be the number three group, who have been grumbling for years that they could cure sooo much cancer and convert so many atheists* if they were just aloud to use Benedictions for non-vampire goals. Once the civil war starts they might just split off into a new group to confuse matters.<br /> <br /> <br /> * I generally run it with the idea that WoD Mortals are so scared/keen to disbelieve magic that if the Pope publically said &quot;Catholic's have Magic biatch!&quot; then cured a bunch of leapers he'd loose followers. But used privately on the right people Benedictions could convert a lot of souls. For example you could walk into a Null Mysteriis meeting and walk out with them all seriously considering that maybe God really does exist. Though on second thoughts that's probably a bad idea because in less than ten minuets someone's going to ask if this implies Ganesha exists too? Then everyone's running to the library to check out all the holy books and see which religion looks like the best one to join as soon as they can determine which gods are real. (Seriously, if I knew gods were real I would definitely start my religious journey by finding out which gods <u>don't</u> send plagues to their followers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 12-17-2013, 07:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-22T14:42:34-08:00","id":35132,"title":"","content":"About the missing catalyst for the Founding: Stalin deported millions into Gulags, where they toiled and died.<br /> These camps were also the forge in which the Russian Mafia was forged. The Order could have arisen there,<br /> out of the need to defend oneself where there was no way to go and no help.<br /> <br /> The Order could have spread to Europe and USA together with the many political or economical refugees.<br /> Russain businesses legal or illegal might need help when dealing with the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Nowadays you might find Compacts of the Order protecting the Russian Orthodox community in New York.<br /> Individual members or Compacts may strike deals or work as advisor for Millionairs or Mafias.<br /> <br /> Love the Compact. Great stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1261-doc-lumbago","name":"Doc Lumbago","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1261_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"57"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}